
ASP.NET EMPLOYEE REGISTRATION FORM WITH VALIDATION CONTROLS
PROJECT SETUP SUMMARY:
- Project Type: ASP.NET Web Application (.NET Framework) -> Empty / Web Forms
- Project Name: EmployeeRegistration


--- STEP 1: CONFIGURE Web.config ---
1. Look at the "Solution Explorer" panel on the right.
2. Double-click the file named "Web.config".
3. Inside the <configuration> tags, add the <appSettings> block shown below.
4. Save the file (Ctrl + S).

--- STEP 2: CREATE EmployeeRegistration.aspx AND EmployeeRegistration.aspx.cs ---
1. Right-click on the project name "EmployeeRegistration" (next to the green globe).
2. Hover over "Add" -> click "New Item...".
3. Under "Visual C#" on the left side, select "Web".
4. From the center list, click "Web Form".
5. Change the name at the bottom to: EmployeeRegistration.aspx
6. Click "Add".
   (Note: This will automatically generate both EmployeeRegistration.aspx and 
    EmployeeRegistration.aspx.cs nested inside it).

--- STEP 3: ADD DESIGN CODE TO EmployeeRegistration.aspx ---
1. Double-click "EmployeeRegistration.aspx" to open it.
2. Select everything (Ctrl + A) and delete it.
3. Paste the complete ASPX markup provided in FILE 2 below.
4. Save the file (Ctrl + S).

--- STEP 4: ADD LOGIC CODE TO EmployeeRegistration.aspx.cs ---
1. In Solution Explorer, click the small arrow (>) next to "EmployeeRegistration.aspx".
2. Double-click "EmployeeRegistration.aspx.cs".
3. Select everything (Ctrl + A) and delete it.
4. Paste the complete C# code provided in FILE 3 below.
5. Save the file (Ctrl + S).

--- STEP 5: RUN AND TEST THE PROJECT ---
1. Right-click "EmployeeRegistration.aspx" in Solution Explorer.
2. Click "Set As Start Page".
3. Press F5 (or click the green Play / "IIS Express" button at the top).

